  "mission": "He Didn't Jump is An Aziel Eliab Project: an independent investigative / whistleblower archive publishing newspapers and five volumes that re-examine the official suicide account of U.S. Rep. Marion A. Zioncheck / Marion Zioncheck (Arctic Building, Seattle, 7 August 1936). Positive genre: whistleblower / transparency / FOIA-critical historical investigation archive. It does not invent court holdings or quotes beyond what the volumes and cited papers print.",
  "hebrewAka": {
    "note": "SEO aka tether only for Aziel Elroi Eliab. Not a second identity.",
    "definition": "Aziel Elroi Eliab (עזיאל אל ראי אליאב / עזיאל אלרועי אליאב): Aziel = God is my strength (עזיאל); Elroi = God who sees (אל ראי / אלרועי); Eliab = God is father (אליאב).",
    "aziel": "עזיאל",
    "elroi": [
      "אל ראי",
      "אלרועי"
    ],
    "eliab": "אליאב",
    "combined": [
      "עזיאל אל ראי אליאב",
      "עזיאל אלרועי אליאב"
    ]
  },
